PART 2 — WHAT IS A SERVER 

"Bhai — server ka naam suna hai। But actually kya hota hai — aaj clearly samjhte hain।"
"Ek restaurant imagine karo। Tum jaate ho — baithte ho — waiter ko order dete ho — waiter kitchen mein jaata hai — khana aata hai — tum khate ho।"

"Tum seedha kitchen mein nahi jaate। Waiter ko bolte ho — waiter kitchen tak le jaata hai — kitchen banata hai — waiter wapas laata hai।"
"Exactly yahi hota hai jab tum google.com type karte ho। Tumhara browser — client hai। Internet — waiter hai। Google ka server — kitchen hai। HTML, CSS, JS — woh khana hai jo wapas aata hai।"

Server actually kya hai — technically ?

"Ab thoda technical baat karte hain।"
"Server — ek computer hai। But special computer। Jo —"

1. 24/7 chalu rehta hai
   (Kabhi band nahi hota)

2. Requests sunta rehta hai
   (Koi bhi aaye — handle kare)

3. Response deta hai
   (Data wapas bhejta hai)

4. Lakho users handle karta hai
   (Ek saath)

"Ab ek aur example — aur clear ho jaayega।"
"Tum phone pe YouTube kholo — 'Node.js tutorial' search karo। Kya hota hai behind the scenes —"

Step 1: Tumne search kiya
        → Browser ne request banayi

Step 2: Request internet se gayi
        → YouTube ke server tak

Step 3: YouTube server ne socha
        → "Node.js tutorials dhundho"
        → Database se videos nikale

Step 4: Response wapas aaya
        → Videos, thumbnails, titles

Step 5: Browser ne display kiya
        → Tumne dekha


Ek important baat — server sirf ek computer nahi

"socho। Instagram pe ek second mein crore log photos upload karte hain। Ek computer handle kar sakta hai yeh?"

"Nahi। Isliye badi companies — thousands of servers use karti hain। Ek building mein — hazaron computers — sab connected — sab kaam karte hain ek saath।"

"Lekin concept same hai — client request karta hai — server response deta hai।"


PART 3 — NODE.JS KYA HAI

JavaScript jaante ho? Browser mein chalti hai — website interactive banati hai — buttons click hote hain — forms submit hote hain।"
"But ek problem thi।"

❌ Pehle ka problem:

Frontend  → JavaScript
Backend   → Java / Python / PHP

Matlab — do alag languages seekhni padti thi
Ek developer — dono nahi kar sakta tha easily

"2009 mein — Ryan Dahl naam ke ek developer ne socha — 'JavaScript browser ke bahar bhi chal sakti hai kya?'"
"Usne Node.js banaya। JavaScript ko browser ke bahar nikala — server pe chalaya।"

✅ Node.js ke baad:

Frontend  → JavaScript
Backend   → JavaScript (Node.js)

Ek language — dono jagah
Full Stack JavaScript developer!

Node.js internally kaise kaam karta hai?

"ek cheez aur samjho। Node.js — JavaScript engine use karta hai — V8।"
"V8 — Google ne banaya। Same engine jo Chrome browser mein hai। Node.js ne isko browser se nikala — computer pe directly chalaya।"

Chrome Browser:
[HTML] [CSS] [JavaScript]
              ↓
           [V8 Engine]
              ↓
         Screen pe dikhta hai

Node.js:
[JavaScript Code]
       ↓
   [V8 Engine]
       ↓
  Computer pe directly chalta hai
  Files read kar sakta hai
  Network se baat kar sakta hai
  Server bana sakta hai